      "title": "My Octopus Teacher",
      "creator": null,
      "note": "Short description: “A filmmaker forges an unusual friendship with an octopus living in a South African kelp forest, learning as the animal shares the mysteries of her world.” Second, [**The Art of Living with Less Stress**](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amS0u15AL14) by [Derek Sivers](https://tim.blog/2015/12/14/derek-sivers-on-developing-confidence-finding-happiness-and-saying-no-to-millions/?utm_source=convertkit&utm_medium=convertkit&utm_campaign=5bf) ([@sivers](https://twitter.com/sivers?lang=en)), which I’m watching repeatedly. The latter might seem odd, as it’s a short clip from a podcast interview I was already part of, but I often choose what I’ll produce (interviews, videos, animations, blog posts, etc.) based on what lessons I most need to revisit. Derek’s stories in this video are currently at the top of my list.",
